      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T18:22:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it is a lot of indirection...\n\nThe goal is for a process to be able to be able to register something once when it\u0027s starting (maybe through an `__attribute((constructor))` library [like this](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/3225466/4/libs/libvm_payload/src/injector.cpp)) and have a way to get binder services over sockets when there is no `servicemanager` process or kernel binder available.\n\nI want to be flexible to allow:\n1) The Accessor binder to come from another process that might die and restart leading to the original Accessor binder to be invalid and never be updated.\n2) Services to become available sometime later. The provider reaches out to some other service and can now create an Accessor for that service when it wouldn\u0027t have been able to when the client process first started.\n\nI think both of these points are probably worth discussing. There may be other reasons to keep it this way but I\u0027m not thinking of them right now. @smoreland@google.com WDYT?\n\nIf we didn\u0027t have #1, it\u0027s going to often be the same as requiring all binder clients to restart when servicemanager crashes/restart. That sounds annoying and unnecessary, but servicemanager is currently `critical` in [its rc file](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/cmds/servicemanager/servicemanager.rc) so we do already do that.\n\nIf we didn\u0027t have #2, it would require knowing all available services as soon as any client starts. This seems like an unnecessary restriction, but again, we do already mostly have this restriction for some subset of binder services.",
      "parentUuid": "6c0fd235_4c162d89",
      "revId": "05491648de2e0e87e060d0a932aad73a6d4e9745",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
